Skip Trichrome expectations validation when secondary ABI is off.

`chrome/android:validate_expectations` is a Chromium android-binary-size
trybot helper. Its `data_deps` hard-code every Trichrome variant —
`_64`, `_32`, `_64_32`, `_32_64` — without checking which ones actually
got instantiated. With `enable_android_secondary_abi = false` the 32-bit
and dual-ABI variants don't exist, and GN's configure phase aborts
with dozens of "needs //chrome/android:trichrome_chrome_32_bundle__...
(does not exist)" errors before any compile starts.

The two switches that gate validate_expectations live in
`chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni`. They're plain
assignments — not `declare_args()` blocks — so they can't be turned
off from `customGnFlags`. Patch them to additionally require
`enable_android_secondary_abi`, so the verifications automatically
disable themselves whenever the dual-ABI variants don't exist. No
effect on the dual-ABI configuration (where the variants do exist
and validation is desirable).

--- a/chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni
+++ b/chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni
@@ -3,12 +3,14 @@
 # found in the LICENSE file.
 #
 import("//build/config/android/config.gni")
+import("//build/config/android/abi.gni")
 import("//build/config/coverage/coverage.gni")
 
 # Chosen to match android-binary-size trybot.
 enable_libs_and_assets_verification =
     !enable_chrome_android_internal && !is_component_build &&
     !use_jacoco_coverage && is_official_build &&
+    enable_android_secondary_abi &&
     ((target_cpu == "arm64" || target_cpu == "x64") &&
      android_channel == "stable")
 
@@ -18,6 +20,7 @@
 # target_cpu: android:versionCode varies.
 enable_manifest_verification =
     !is_java_debug && !enable_chrome_android_internal && !use_jacoco_coverage &&
+    enable_android_secondary_abi &&
     ((target_cpu == "arm64" || target_cpu == "x64") &&
      android_channel == "stable")
